/-!
# The blowup of an affine chart in the product of its determinantal ideals

Let `(X, D, M)` be a triple as in Situation 0F8S and let `(U, A, f, M^•)` be an affine chart for
it.  Stacks tag 0GTY blows `U` up in the product `I = ∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the determinantal
ideals of the chart, and asserts of the resulting morphism `b_U : U' ⟶ U` that it is a
`(U \ D)`-admissible blowing up and that the triple pulled back along it is good.

This file proves both of those assertions, over a single affine chart.  The algebraic heart is
that the inverse image of each individual factor `I_i(M^•, f)` to `U'` is an effective Cartier
divisor: that is the step the tag's proof takes from Divisors, Lemmas 31.33.12 and 31.33.4 — the
blowup in a product factors through the blowup in each factor, on which that factor becomes
invertible.  Goodness of the pulled-back triple follows, the pulled-back chart of part (1) of
Stacks tag 0F8T having exactly those inverse images as its determinantal ideals.

What is *not* here is the gluing of the `b_U` over a basis of charts into a single `b : X' ⟶ X`,
which is the existence half of clauses (1) and (2) of the tag, nor the admissibility over a
general quasi-compact open.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.determinantalIdealSheaf`: the
  determinantal ideal `I_i(M^•, f)` of a chart, read as an ideal sheaf on the affine open
  subscheme `U` rather than as an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`.

## Main results

* `AffineChart.blowupCentreIdealSheaf_eq_prod`: the centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup, as an
  ideal sheaf on `U`, is the product of the `I_i(M^•, f)` as ideal sheaves on `U`.
* `AffineChart.isAdmissibleBlowup_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf`: **Stacks tag 0GTY, the
  admissibility assertion over an affine chart.**  The blowing up of `U` in `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` is a
  `(U \ D)`-admissible blowing up.
* `AffineChart.preimage_compl_support_eq_basicOpen`: the part of the chart off the divisor is the
  standard open of the equation `f`.
* `AffineChart.isProper_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf`: that blowing up is proper over the
  chart, the centre being of finite type (`AffineChart.fg_ideal_blowupCentreIdealSheaf`).
* `AffineChart.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf`: the inverse image of
  each factor `I_i(M^•, f)` to the blowup `U'` is an effective Cartier divisor.
* `AffineChart.exists_isPrincipal_ideal_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf`: hence it is, around every
  point of `U'`, generated by a single element on a suitable affine open.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_affineOpen_forall_isPrincipal`: finitely many locally principal ideal
  sheaves are simultaneously principal on one affine open around any point.
* `AffineChart.chartBlowupToBase`: the composite `U' ⟶ U ⟶ X`, which is what the morphism `b` of
  the tag restricts to over the chart.
* `AffineChart.isGoodOver_comp_ι`: a morphism to the chart along which each `I_i(M^•, f)` becomes
  an effective Cartier divisor is good for the triple.
* `AffineChart.isGoodOver_chartBlowupToBase`: **Stacks tag 0GTY, clause (1) over an affine
  chart.**  That composite is good for the triple: the pullback of `D` along it is defined and the
  pulled-back triple is a good triple.

## Implementation notes

The two conditions in the definition of a `(U \ D)`-admissible blowing up are finite presentation
of the centre and disjointness of its support from `U \ D`; both are read off the two facts about
the centre already proved in `GoodTriple.lean`, that it is of finite type and that it contains a
power of the equation `f` of the divisor.  Disjointness goes through the inverse image
`D ∩ U = (D).comap U.ι` of the divisor: a power of it is contained in the centre, so the support
of the centre is contained in the support of `D ∩ U` by antitonicity, which is disjoint from the
complement of `D`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop` turns an ideal of `Γ(U, ⊤)` into an ideal
sheaf on `U`; it is multiplicative — this is checked ideal by ideal on the affine opens of `U`,
with `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_finsetProd_eq_prod` and `Ideal.map_finset_prod` — which is what
identifies the ideal sheaf of the centre with the product of the ideal sheaves of the factors.
That identification is what lets
`AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_of_mem_prod` — a factor of a product whose
inverse image is an effective Cartier divisor has itself an effective Cartier inverse image — be
applied to the exceptional divisor of the blowup.

Both `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp` and `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp` are available; the chart's blowup is
taken at the latter, as `AffineChart.blowupCentreIdealSheaf` is, and
`Stacks.Blowup.isAdmissibleBlowup_iff` is the form of the definition of admissibility stated at
that spelling.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GTY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GTY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F8S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F8S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080A)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory

universe u d

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The extension of a finite product of ideals along a ring homomorphism is the product of the
extensions of the factors. -/
theorem Ideal.map_finset_prod {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B)
    {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (J : ι → Ideal A) :
    Ideal.map φ (∏ i ∈ s, J i) = ∏ i ∈ s, Ideal.map φ (J i) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simpa only [Finset.prod_empty, Ideal.one_eq_top] using Ideal.map_top φ
  | insert a t ha ih => rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, Finset.prod_insert ha, Ideal.map_mul, ih]

namespace ComplexAndDivisorSituation

namespace AffineChart

variable {S : ComplexAndDivisorSituation.{u, d}}

/-- **The determinantal ideal `I_i(M^•, f)` of an affine chart, read as an ideal sheaf on the
affine open subscheme `U`** rather than as an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`.  The product of these over the
degrees in which `M^•` is nonzero is the centre
`AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexAndDivisorSituation.AffineChart.blowupCentreIdealSheaf` in which Stacks
tag 0GTY blows the chart up. -/
def determinantalIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) (i : ℤ) : C.U.1.toScheme.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop ((C.determinantalIdeal i).map C.U.1.topIso.inv.hom)

/-- **The centre of the blowup of an affine chart is the product of the ideal sheaves of its
determinantal ideals.**  Taking the ideal sheaf on `U` of an ideal of `Γ(X, U)` is multiplicative,
and so is extending an ideal along the identification `Γ(X, U) ≅ Γ(U, ⊤)`. -/
theorem blowupCentreIdealSheaf_eq_prod (C : AffineChart S) :
    C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf =
      ∏ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset, C.determinantalIdealSheaf i := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext (funext fun U => ?_)
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_finsetProd_eq_prod, blowupCentreIdealSheaf,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, blowupCentre, Ideal.map_finset_prod,
    Ideal.map_finset_prod]
  exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => by
    rw [determinantalIdealSheaf, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal]

/-- On an affine scheme the ideal sheaf of an ideal of the global sections has that ideal as its
ideal on the whole scheme. -/
private theorem ofIdealTop_ideal_top {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine X] (J : Ideal Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop J).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top X⟩ = J := by
  simp [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal]

/-- **A power of the inverse image of the divisor to an affine chart lies in the centre of the
blowup.**  The centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` contains `f ^ (∑ᵢ rᵢ)`, hence also the next power of `f`,
and the inverse image of `D` to `U` is cut out by `f`. -/
theorem pow_comap_D_le_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) :
    S.D.comap (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι ^ ((∑ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset, C.complex.rank i) + 1) ≤
      C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf := by
  let : IsAffine (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme := C.U.2
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_of_isAffine ?_
  have hpow : C.f ^ ((∑ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset, C.complex.rank i) + 1) ∈
      C.blowupCentre := by
    rw [pow_succ']
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ C.pow_mem_blowupCentre
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow, Pi.pow_apply,
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE S.D (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι C.U
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ (by simp), Scheme.Opens.ι_appLE_top, C.divisor_ideal, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton, Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff,
    blowupCentreIdealSheaf, ofIdealTop_ideal_top]
  rw [← map_pow]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hpow

/-- **The centre of the blowup of an affine chart is supported on the divisor.**  A power of the
inverse image of `D` to `U` lies in the centre, so the support of the centre is contained in that
of `D ∩ U`, which is disjoint from `U \ D`.  This is one of the two conditions for the blowing up
of the chart in that centre to be a `(U \ D)`-admissible blowing up. -/
theorem disjoint_support_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) :
    Disjoint
      (((C.U : S.X.Opens).ι ⁻¹ᵁ S.D.support.compl : (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme.Opens) :
        Set (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme)
      (C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf.support : Set (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) := by
  refine Disjoint.mono_right
    (?_ : (C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf.support : Set (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) ≤
      ((S.D.comap (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι ^
        ((∑ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset, C.complex.rank i) + 1)).support :
          Set (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme)) ?_
  · exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_antitone C.pow_comap_D_le_blowupCentreIdealSheaf
  · rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_pow_succ, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
    exact Disjoint.preimage _ disjoint_compl_left

/-- The centre `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the blowup of an affine chart, read as an ideal sheaf on the
open subscheme `U`, is of finite type: on every affine open of `U` it is the extension of the
finitely generated ideal `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f) ⊂ Γ(X, U)`. -/
theorem fg_ideal_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S)
    (V : (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme.affineOpens) : (C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf.ideal V).FG := by
  rw [blowupCentreIdealSheaf, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal]
  exact (C.blowupCentre_fg.map _).map _

/-- **The centre of the blowup of an affine chart is of finite presentation.**  Its ideal on any
affine open of `U` is an extension of the finitely generated ideal `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)`, hence
finitely generated, which is the affine-local criterion of Stacks tag 01TV.  This is the other
condition for the blowing up of the chart in that centre to be a `(U \ D)`-admissible blowing
up. -/
theorem finitePresentation_subschemeι_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) :
    FinitePresentation C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf.subschemeι := by
  rw [finitePresentation_subschemeι_iff_isFiniteType]
  exact C.fg_ideal_blowupCentreIdealSheaf

/-- **Stacks tag 0GTY, the admissibility assertion over an affine chart.**  Over an affine chart
`(U, A, f, M^•)` the morphism `b` of the tag is the blowing up of `U` in the product
`∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of the determinantal ideals of the chart, and that blowing up is a
`(U \ D)`-admissible blowing up: the centre is of finite presentation and its support, being
contained in that of `D ∩ U`, is disjoint from `U \ D`. -/
@[stacks 0GTY "the admissibility assertion over an affine chart: the blowing up of the chart in \
the product of its determinantal ideals, which is what `b` restricts to there, is a \
`(U \\ D)`-admissible blowing up"]
theorem isAdmissibleBlowup_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) :
    Stacks.Blowup.IsAdmissibleBlowup
      ((C.U : S.X.Opens).ι ⁻¹ᵁ S.D.support.compl)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) :=
  (Stacks.Blowup.isAdmissibleBlowup_iff _ _).mpr
    ⟨C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf, C.finitePresentation_subschemeι_blowupCentreIdealSheaf,
      C.disjoint_support_blowupCentreIdealSheaf, Iso.refl _, Category.id_comp _⟩

/-- **The part of an affine chart off the divisor is the standard open of the equation.**  A
point of `U` lies on `D` exactly when the equation `f` of `D ∩ U` vanishes there, since `f`
generates the ideal of `D` on `U`. -/
theorem preimage_compl_support_eq_basicOpen (C : AffineChart S) :
    (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι ⁻¹ᵁ S.D.support.compl
      = (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme.basicOpen ((C.U : S.X.Opens).topIso.inv.hom C.f) := by
  refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext (Set.ext fun y => ?_)
  obtain ⟨x, hxU⟩ := y
  have hsupp : x ∈ S.D.support ↔ x ∉ S.X.basicOpen C.f := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := C.U) hxU, C.divisor_ideal,
      Scheme.zeroLocus_span, Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton, Set.mem_compl_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
  have hbase := Stacks.Divisors.mem_basicOpen_topIso_inv_iff (C.U : S.X.Opens) C.f x hxU
  exact ⟨fun hy => hbase.2 (of_not_not fun hb => hy (hsupp.2 hb)),
    fun hy hc => hsupp.1 hc (hbase.1 hy)⟩

/-- The blowing up of an affine chart in the product of its determinantal ideals is proper over
the chart: the centre is of finite type. -/
theorem isProper_blowUpToBase_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) :
    IsProper (Stacks.Blowup.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) :=
  Stacks.Blowup.isProper_blowUpToBase _ C.fg_ideal_blowupCentreIdealSheaf

/-- **Each determinantal ideal of an affine chart becomes an effective Cartier divisor on the
blowup of the chart in their product.**  This is the step of the proof of Stacks tag 0GTY that
cites Divisors, Lemmas 31.33.12 and 31.33.4: the inverse image of the whole product is the
exceptional divisor of the blowup, hence an effective Cartier divisor by tag 02OS, and a factor of
an effective Cartier divisor is one by tag 07ZV. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) {i : ℤ}
    (hi : i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      ((C.determinantalIdealSheaf i).comap
        (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf)) :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_of_mem_prod _ _ _
    (C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf_eq_prod ▸
      Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) hi

/-- **Around every point of the blowup of an affine chart, each determinantal ideal of the chart
becomes principal.**  Its inverse image is an effective Cartier divisor, which affine-locally is
generated by a nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem exists_isPrincipal_ideal_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) {i : ℤ}
    (hi : i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset)
    (y : AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf) :
    ∃ V : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf).affineOpens, y ∈ (V : Set _) ∧
      (((C.determinantalIdealSheaf i).comap
        (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf)).ideal V).IsPrincipal := by
  obtain ⟨V, hyV, t, -, ht⟩ := Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_isRegular _
    (C.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf hi) y
  exact ⟨V, hyV, ht ▸ ⟨t, rfl⟩⟩

/-! ### Simultaneous local principality -/

/-- Principality of the ideal of an ideal sheaf on an affine open passes to a smaller affine
open, the ideal there being the extension of the ideal here. -/
private theorem isPrincipal_ideal_of_le {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    {V W : X.affineOpens} (h : V ≤ W) (hW : (I.ideal W).IsPrincipal) :
    (I.ideal V).IsPrincipal := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hW
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal I h, ht, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  exact ⟨_, rfl⟩

/-- **Finitely many locally principal ideal sheaves are simultaneously principal on a single
affine open around any point.**  Each is principal on some affine neighbourhood; an affine open
inside the finite intersection of those neighbourhoods works for all of them at once, principality
passing to a smaller affine open. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_forall_isPrincipal {X : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type*}
    (s : Finset ι) (J : ι → X.IdealSheafData)
    (h : ∀ i ∈ s, Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal (J i)) (y : X) :
    ∃ V : X.affineOpens, y ∈ (V : Set X) ∧ ∀ i ∈ s, ((J i).ideal V).IsPrincipal := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
    obtain ⟨-, ⟨V, hVaff, rfl⟩, hyV, -⟩ :=
      X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ y) isOpen_univ
    exact ⟨⟨V, hVaff⟩, hyV, by simp⟩
  | insert a t ha ih =>
    obtain ⟨V, hyV, hVt⟩ := ih fun i hi => h i (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi)
    obtain ⟨W, hyW, hWa⟩ := h a (Finset.mem_insert_self a t) y
    obtain ⟨-, ⟨Z, hZaff, rfl⟩, hyZ, hZle⟩ :=
      X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
        (show y ∈ (((V : X.Opens) ⊓ (W : X.Opens) : X.Opens) : Set X) from ⟨hyV, hyW⟩)
        ((V : X.Opens) ⊓ (W : X.Opens)).isOpen
    have hZV : (⟨Z, hZaff⟩ : X.affineOpens) ≤ V := fun x hx => (hZle hx).1
    have hZW : (⟨Z, hZaff⟩ : X.affineOpens) ≤ W := fun x hx => (hZle hx).2
    refine ⟨⟨Z, hZaff⟩, hyZ, fun i hi => ?_⟩
    rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hi with rfl | hit
    · exact isPrincipal_ideal_of_le _ hZW hWa
    · exact isPrincipal_ideal_of_le _ hZV (hVt i hit)

/-! ### Goodness of the chart's blowup -/

/-- **The morphism `b_U : U' ⟶ X` of Stacks tag 0GTY over an affine chart**: the blowing up of
the chart `(U, A, f, M^•)` in the product `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of its determinantal ideals, followed
by the inclusion of `U` into `X`. -/
abbrev chartBlowupToBase (C : AffineChart S) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf ⟶ S.X :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι

/-- **The pullback of `D` along the blowup of an affine chart is defined.**  It factors as the
pullback to `U`, which is defined because the inclusion of an open subscheme is flat, followed by
the pullback along the blowup morphism, which is defined by Stacks tag 0809. -/
theorem isPullbackDefined_chartBlowupToBase (C : AffineChart S) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined C.chartBlowupToBase S.D := by
  change Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (S.D.comap C.chartBlowupToBase)
  rw [chartBlowupToBase, Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp]
  exact isPullbackDefined_blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf
    (S.D.comap (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) (S.isPullbackDefined_ι (C.U : S.X.Opens))

/-- The map on sections induced by a morphism into the affine open of a chart followed by the
inclusion of that open is the identification `Γ(X, U) ≅ Γ(U, ⊤)` followed by the map on sections
induced by the morphism itself. -/
private theorem comp_ι_appLE (C : AffineChart S) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : Z ⟶ (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) (V : Z.Opens)
    (hV : V ≤ (b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) ⁻¹ᵁ (C.U : S.X.Opens)) (h' : V ≤ b ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤) :
    (b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι).appLE (C.U : S.X.Opens) V hV
      = (C.U : S.X.Opens).topIso.inv ≫ b.appLE ⊤ V h' := by
  rw [← Scheme.Opens.ι_appLE_top (C.U : S.X.Opens) (by simp), Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE]

/-- **The inverse image of an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`, read as an ideal sheaf on `U`, along a morphism
into `U`.**  On an affine open `V` of the source it is the extension of the ideal along the map on
sections induced by `V ⟶ U ⟶ X`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_ofIdealTop_map_topIso (C : AffineChart S) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : Z ⟶ (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) (V : Z.affineOpens) (J : Ideal Γ(S.X, C.U))
    (hV : (V : Z.Opens) ≤ (b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) ⁻¹ᵁ (C.U : S.X.Opens)) :
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (J.map (C.U : S.X.Opens).topIso.inv.hom)).comap b).ideal V
      = Ideal.map ((b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι).appLE
          (C.U : S.X.Opens) (V : Z.Opens) hV).hom J := by
  let : IsAffine (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme := C.U.2
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE _ b ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ V (by simp),
    ofIdealTop_ideal_top, Ideal.map_map,
    comp_ι_appLE C b (V : Z.Opens) hV (by simp), CommRingCat.hom_comp]

/-- **The inverse image of a chart's determinantal ideal sheaf computes the determinantal ideal
of the pulled-back chart.**  Both are the extension of `I_i(M^•, f)` along the map on sections
induced by `V ⟶ U ⟶ X`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : Z ⟶ (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) (V : Z.affineOpens) (i : ℤ)
    (hV : (V : Z.Opens) ≤ (b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) ⁻¹ᵁ (C.U : S.X.Opens)) :
    ((C.determinantalIdealSheaf i).comap b).ideal V
      = Ideal.map ((b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι).appLE
          (C.U : S.X.Opens) (V : Z.Opens) hV).hom (C.determinantalIdeal i) :=
  C.ideal_comap_ofIdealTop_map_topIso b V (C.determinantalIdeal i) hV

/-- **The inverse image of the centre of the blowup of a chart.**  On an affine open `V` of the
source it is the extension of `∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` along the map on sections induced by
`V ⟶ U ⟶ X`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_blowupCentreIdealSheaf (C : AffineChart S) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : Z ⟶ (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme) (V : Z.affineOpens)
    (hV : (V : Z.Opens) ≤ (b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) ⁻¹ᵁ (C.U : S.X.Opens)) :
    (C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf.comap b).ideal V
      = Ideal.map ((b ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι).appLE
          (C.U : S.X.Opens) (V : Z.Opens) hV).hom C.blowupCentre :=
  C.ideal_comap_ofIdealTop_map_topIso b V C.blowupCentre hV

/-- **A morphism to an affine chart along which every determinantal ideal of the chart becomes an
effective Cartier divisor is good for the triple.**  Let `(U, A, f, M^•)` be an affine chart and
let `q : Z ⟶ U` be a morphism along which the pullback of `D` is defined and the inverse image of
each `I_i(M^•, f)` is an effective Cartier divisor.  Then `Z ⟶ U ⟶ X` is good for the triple.

Every point of `Z` lies in an affine open `V` on which all the finitely many inverse images
`I_i(M^•, f)𝒪_Z` are principal, those being effective Cartier divisors by hypothesis; the degrees
in which `M^•` vanishes contribute the unit ideal.  By part (1) of Stacks tag 0F8T such a `V`
carries the pulled-back chart `(V, Γ(Z, V), f|_V, M^• ⊗_A Γ(Z, V))`, and by part (2) of that tag
its determinantal ideals are exactly those inverse images. -/
theorem isGoodOver_comp_ι (C : AffineChart S) {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (q : Z ⟶ (C.U : S.X.Opens).toScheme)
    (hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined (q ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) S.D)
    (hcart : ∀ i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset,
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor ((C.determinantalIdealSheaf i).comap q)) :
    S.IsGoodOver (q ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) where
  pullbackDefined := hD
  isGoodTriple := by
    classical
    rintro y -
    obtain ⟨V, hyV, hprin⟩ := exists_affineOpen_forall_isPrincipal
      C.complex.bounded.toFinset
      (fun i => (C.determinantalIdealSheaf i).comap q)
      (fun i hi => Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.isLocallyPrincipal _ (hcart i hi)) y
    refine ⟨C.pullback (q ≫ (C.U : S.X.Opens).ι) hD V (by simp), hyV,
      fun i => ?_⟩
    rw [C.pullback_determinantalIdeal]
    by_cases hi : i ∈ C.complex.bounded.toFinset
    · rw [← C.ideal_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf q V i (by simp)]
      exact hprin i hi
    · have hr : C.complex.rank i = 0 := by
        simpa only [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, not_not] using hi
      rw [C.determinantalIdeal_eq_top hr, Ideal.map_top]
      exact ⟨1, Ideal.span_singleton_one.symm⟩

/-- **Stacks tag 0GTY, clause (1) over an affine chart.**  Let `(U, A, f, M^•)` be an affine
chart for the triple `(X, D, M)` and let `b_U : U' ⟶ U` be the blowing up of `U` in the product
`∏ᵢ I_i(M^•, f)` of its determinantal ideals.  Then the composite `U' ⟶ U ⟶ X` is good for the
triple: the pullback of `D` along it is defined, and the pulled-back triple
`(U', b_U⁻¹(D ∩ U), Lb_U^*M)` is a good triple.

Every point of `U'` lies in an affine open `V` on which all the finitely many inverse images
`I_i(M^•, f)𝒪_{U'}` are principal, these being effective Cartier divisors by
`AffineChart.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf`; the degrees in which `M^•`
vanishes contribute the unit ideal.  By part (1) of Stacks tag 0F8T such a `V` carries the
pulled-back chart `(V, Γ(U', V), f|_V, M^• ⊗_A Γ(U', V))`, and by part (2) of that tag its
determinantal ideals are exactly those inverse images. -/
@[stacks 0GTY "clause (1) over an affine chart: the triple pulled back along the blowing up of \
the chart in the product of its determinantal ideals --- which is what `b` restricts to over the \
chart --- is a good triple, and the pullback of `D` along it is defined"]
theorem isGoodOver_chartBlowupToBase (C : AffineChart S) :
    S.IsGoodOver C.chartBlowupToBase :=
  C.isGoodOver_comp_ι (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase C.blowupCentreIdealSheaf)
    C.isPullbackDefined_chartBlowupToBase
    fun _ hi => C.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_determinantalIdealSheaf hi

end AffineChart

end ComplexAndDivisorSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

